    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n91502" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πύλος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῠ], ὁ</span>
		and ἡ
		<u>Pylos</u>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν Π. ἠγαθέῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.252
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πύλου ἱερῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					21.108
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				5.70
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1058
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.39
			</span></i>, etc.; but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Π. ἠμαθόεντος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.77
				</span></i>
			, al., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				360
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέγεται καὶ θηλυκῶς καὶ ἀρσενικῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					St.Byz.
				</span></i>
			: masc. in <i><span class="en">Str., 8.3.26</span></i>
			(sg. and pl.), al.</div>
